caption:
🚨 SOUTH AFRICANS ARE BEING DISPLACED IN THEIR OWN COUNTRY

@dada_morero and Mlungisi Mabaso, the pain and frustration in Ward 100, Cosmo City is impossible to ignore. Families say they have been denied homes meant for them while illegal occupation continues. Every South African deserves a fair chance and ActionSA will advocate for them to get one. 

 We'll be live during the mayoral oversight. Stay tuned.

@action4sa Joburg MMC: Group Coporate and Shared Services Candidate, Nandi Ndaba joined Ward 112 Green Saturday Blitz led by Candidate Councilor Cllr. Khomo Mashala in Carlswald Shopping Centre. 

#OperationFixJoburg 
#MashabaForMayor

ALLOCATED ON RECORDS, ABANDONED IN REALITY!
@action4sa MMC Candidate for Human Settlements led an oversight in Plot 8 alongside fellow candidates. Residents say their RDP houses are allocated on the system, yet in reality they still live in dire conditions. 

#OperationFixJoburg

@action4sa MMC Candidate for Human Settlements, Zandile Dabula hearing out devastated Fleurhof residents who say they were dumped into overcrowded flats after being removed from their homes. Women forced to share with unknown men, while other families sleep outside in the cold. Joburg Residents Deserve Better!! 

#OperationFixJoburg
#MashabaForMayor

@action4sa has just published the full declassified Phala Phala investigation report.

South Africans demanded the full truth, and we fought for it. Now, we will fight for accountability!

Full report on ActionSA's website.

This Thursday - 5 February 2026 - marks 10 long years since the tragic collapse of Lily Mine in Barberton, Mpumalanga. 

@action4sa will continue to stand in solidarity with the Lily Mine victims' families in their fight for closure and justice.

#JusticeForLilyMine

@action4sa stands with its Ekurhuleni Mayoral Candidate, @xkhumalo_. 

We will not allow crime fighters to be intimidated by the corrupt cops, while criminals are allowed to freely operate in our communities.

#HandsOffXolani

The DA’s latest attempt to mislead Tshwane residents with its so-called “R777m water tanker exposé” is a deliberate political lie.

@action4sa  rejects this cheap political opportunism and stands behind the forensic investigation ordered by the Mayor.

🔗 https://www.actionsa.org.za/actionsa-slams-das-lies-over-the-myth-of-the-r777-million/

We are out in Soweto Ward 29 engaging with residents, and the message is clear: The people are ready for real change!

@action4sa’s Josiah “Coach” Moloi is ready to lead and serve.

Let’s make it happen, Soweto Ward 29. #VoteActionSA and Josiah “Coach” Moloi.

@action4sa Soweto Ward 130 By-election Candidate Siyabonga Zwane has a plan to serve his community and deliver real change.

Soweto Ward 130 residents, it's time for ACTION. 

#VoteActionSA and Siyabonga Zwane tomorrow.

As the Mayor of Joburg, I led a government that got to work fixing the basics.

We prioritised upgrading ageing water infrastructure and replacing crumbling sewage lines.

@action4sa is ready to propose suitable leaders to do this needed work nationwide!

@action4sa leads the 9th Commemoration of the Lily Mine Tragedy, alongside the families of the three deceased mineworkers - Pretty Nkambule, Yvonne Mnisi, and Solomon Nyirenda.

Join us live on ActionSA's YouTube Channel! 

#JusticeForLilyMine

@action4sa's bold agenda for 2025. 

